# Line endings are LF everywhere, including Windows working trees.
#
# Without this, Git's core.autocrlf checks files out with CRLF on Windows, and the formatter then
# reports every file as needing a rewrite — which is exactly how the Windows CI job failed the first
# time it ran. Normalising here fixes it for contributors too: no spurious whole-file diffs, and no
# rewritten results.json after running the golden path.
#
# If a genuinely CRLF-only file is ever added (a .cmd or .bat script), give it an explicit
# `text eol=crlf` rule rather than relaxing this one.
* text=auto eol=lf
